course: dictionary
lesson: 11230
title: Tricky place names
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Worcestershire is a county in the West Midlands of England, and its main city is Worcester. The name also goes on a dark, tangy, spicy sauce that was first made in Worcester.
explain: The name is a puzzle because it does not sound the way it is spelled. «Worcestershire is said "WUSS-ter-sher", Leicester "LES-ter" and Gloucester "GLOS-ter".» You cannot sound it out, so you have to learn it.
explain: Place names often keep their old spelling while speech shortens them. For how to say a place name, listen to the people who live there. For what a word means, read the words around it.
fact: Worcestershire is a county in the West Midlands of England.
fact: Worcestershire sauce is a dark, tangy, spicy sauce first made in Worcester.
fact: Worcestershire sauce is used on food and in cooking, for example in stews, on cheese on toast and in a Caesar salad.
fact: Worcestershire is said "WUSS-ter-sher", not the way it is spelled.
fact: For place names, listen to the locals to learn how to say them.
exercise: «Worcestershire is said "WUSS-ter-sher", Leicester "LES-ter" and Gloucester "GLOS-ter".» How is Worcestershire said? | WOR-kes-ter-sheer | WOR-ces-ter-shire | WUR-ches-ter-shur | *WUSS-ter-sher
exercise: In geography, what is Worcestershire? | *A county in England | A river in Wales | A type of cheese | A city in Scotland
exercise: Which food might use Worcestershire sauce? | Orange juice | Plain boiled rice with nothing else | Sliced bananas in a bowl | *Cheese on toast
test: Which city was Worcestershire sauce first made in? | Leicester | Gloucester | *Worcester | Malvern
test: «Names keep their spelling while speech shortens them.» What does this tell you? | Names never change at all | Only sauces have tricky names | Place names are always spelled how they sound | *Spelling and speech can differ, so you must learn how a name is said
exam: How should you find out how to say a tricky place name? | Skip the name and never read it | Guess from the spelling | Ask the sauce bottle | *Listen to the people who live there
